      "name": {
        "name": "Zinc transporter Msc2-like",
        "short": "Msc2-like"
      },
      "description": [
        {
          "text": "<p>This entry represents a group of metal transporters, including Msc2 from budding yeasts, Cis4 from fission yeasts, SLC30A5/7 (also known as ZNT7/5) from humans and MTPC2/MTP12 from Arabidopsis. They are zinc transporters involved in zinc ion homeostasis [[cite:PUB00098538], [cite:PUB00098539], [cite:PUB00098540], [cite:PUB00098541]]. ZNT5/7 in the early secretory pathway, regulate the activation and folding of enzymes like alkaline phosphatases and enzymes involved in phosphatidylinositol glycan anchor biosynthesis [[cite:PUB00101859]].</p>",
          "llm": false,
          "checked": false,
          "updated": false
        }
      ],
